- runtime/somart/codec.py      NumPy port of motionbricks/model/soma/kernels.py and
                               motionbricks/model/kernels.py (encode, decode, conditions,
                               endpoint correction)
- runtime/somart/skeleton.py   BVH loading logic ported from motionbricks/io/bvh.py
- runtime/somart/contract.py   constants from motionbricks/model/contract.py and soma_n1.json

The upstream ONNX exporter (tools/onnx) is used unmodified from third_party/ (not redistributed).
Changes relative to upstream: vectorised NumPy implementation, batching, and the additional
velocity-matching and contact-aware options in codec.py.

Model weights: NVIDIA Open Model Agreement ("Licensed by NVIDIA Corporation under the NVIDIA Open
Model License"). site/models/ holds an INT8-quantized derivative (int8/FP16 weight storage) for the web demo.
Sample motion clips: NVIDIA Sample Data Evaluation License. The clips are not redistributed here;
site/data/windows.* contains motion windows derived from them (internal evaluation use).
SOMA body mesh (site/data/soma_mesh.*): extracted from the upstream MotionBricks asset
soma_base_skel_minimal_no_root.usd, NVIDIA, CC BY 4.0.

site/vendor/ redistributes, unmodified: onnxruntime-web 1.31.1 (Microsoft, MIT), three.js 0.170.0
